  "narrative": [
    "All major requirements for each degree program must be completed with a C– or better, except for courses offered Pass/No Pass only.",
    "All major requirements and upper-division electives except CSE 91, 95, 109, 197, 198, or 199 must be taken for a letter grade.",
    "To graduate, a minimum grade point average of 2.0 will be required in upper-division courses in the major, including upper-division electives.",
    "At most four units of CSE 197 may be used toward technical elective requirements.",
    "CSE 195 cannot be used toward course requirements.",
    "Students may not get duplicate credit for equivalent courses.",
    "Selective major: admission for continuing students is by selective major application (screening courses: CSE 8B or 11, CSE 12, CSE 29 or ECE 15 or CSE 15L, CSE 20, CSE 21, CSE 30 or ECE 30, CSE 100 (R), and CSE 101 for applicants after second year).",
    "The BS computer engineering program requires a total of 132 units (not including the general-education requirements).",
    "The BS computer engineering program is jointly administered by the Departments of Computer Science and Engineering and Electrical and Computer Engineering.",
    "Students must complete sixty-four upper-division units: eight units of CSE core courses, twelve units of ECE core courses, four CSE or ECE project course units, and forty units of elective courses.",
    "All courses must be taken for a letter grade unless they are offered P/NP only.",
    "The ECE page (catalog.ucsd.edu/curric/ECE-ug.html) describes the same curriculum with differences: it prints 'required to take CSE 140, CSE 141, or CSE 142' with a 68-unit upper-division total, lists MATH 18 and 20A-B-C-D without the MATH 31AH/31BH alternatives, and allows a maximum of four units of P/NP courses (CSE 198, 199, 199H, ECE 191, 193H, 196, 198, 199). This file follows the CSE page, whose unit breakdown (8 units of CSE core, 64 upper-division units, 132 total) fits CSE 140 plus one of CSE 141/142."
